    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** serving as the undisputed anchor of the lineup. With a 77.38 score, his matchup against Roupp is the prime target; the combination of a favorable RHP matchup and a top-tier batting order position (#2) allows him to leverage his elite speed, which remains our primary focus in this 5x5 format. Similarly, **Josh Naylor** (65.29) and **Austin Riley** (64.31) provide the core power upside. While **Austin Riley** faces a favorable park factor, his elevated score is largely driven by the dismal 9.71 xERA of Garrett, turning this into a potential breakout game for our 3B. **Mickey Moniak** also projects as a strong play (60.24) despite a disadvantageous platoon split, as his park environment is simply too favorable to ignore, keeping his floor high enough to warrant the start.\n\nStrategic bench decisions were dictated by efficiency, with **Vinnie Pasquantino** (43.31) representing the closest call for exclusion. While his raw metrics are solid, the negative platoon impact against Suarez pushed him into our bottom tier, barely outpacing our other utility options. **Brice Turang** (55.48) remains a critical inclusion over pure power threats because of his dual-threat potential; the combination of a high batting order position and the ability to exploit slow pitcher deliveries for stolen bases keeps his value high even when his direct SP matchup looks moderate. \n\nWe are monitoring two specific risks today: the elite arm of McLean, which suppresses the score for **James Wood** (52.66), and the general volatility of our bench depth. With **Jose Caballero**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, and **Trevor Story** remaining sidelined, our roster flexibility is restricted, forcing us to lean heavily on the current active starters. **Gabriel Moreno** and **Travis Bazzana** sit right on the cusp of our \"Strong\" tier (55.10 and 55.03, respectively); they are essentially \"hold\" plays for today, serving as high-floor fillers while we wait for the offense to cycle through the more favorable matchups presented by **Corbin Carroll** and **Josh Naylor**.",
